WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.963
(upbeat music)

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:06.360
- Hey Wisecrack, Michael here.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.140
Today we're talking about
a nearly 22 year-old game

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:10.830
that still gives us nightmares,

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:13.540
the PS2 horror classic, Silent Hill 2.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.100
Often ranked as among the
greatest games ever made,

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.220
not just in horror,

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.700
it is influential for other
games and films as well.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.430
Even Guillermo del Toro
confesses to being a fan.

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:25.890
- Because it's one of my
favorite gaming franchises

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:27.680
and story-telling franchises ever.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.600
- So what makes it so great?

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:31.219
And why did its successors which borrowed

00:00:31.219 --> 00:00:34.530
so heavily from it,
not quite hit the mark?

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:37.020
Well, it has a lot to do
with the psychological part

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:38.720
of its psychological horror.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.260
So turn on your radios
and grab a plank of wood

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:42.500
for this Wisecrack edition

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.660
on the Psychology of Silent Hill 2.

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:47.710
And spoilers ahead for an old video game.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:49.380
Let's do a quick recap.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:52.230
Silent Hill 2 is the story
of widowed James Sunderland,

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:54.390
who arrives at the titular
town of Silent Hill

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:56.750
after receiving a letter
from his wife, Mary,

00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:58.070
asking for him to visit.

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:01.000
But Mary's been dead for three years.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.430
- [James] A dead person
can't write a letter.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:06.830
Mary died of that damn
disease three years ago.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:08.930
- [Michael] So James is
understandably confused,

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:10.310
and decides to investigate.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:12.810
Upon arrival, a pretty mean fog rolls in

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:15.540
that hides some grotesque
monsters and draw distances.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:18.060
He soon realizes the town is nearly empty

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:19.690
save for nightmare fuel.

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:22.490
He does, however, meet some normal people.

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:23.800
Well, sort of normal.

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:25.760
The schlub-with-a-stomach-bug, Eddie,

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:27.570
the lost and erratic Angela,

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:30.280
and the really obnoxious
little girl, Laura.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:32.730
None of whom are all that
interested in hanging out

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:34.110
or being particularly helpful,

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:36.600
like when Laura locks
James in a room to die.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:37.433
- [James] Laura!

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:40.380
What are you doing?

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:41.550
- [Michael] James also witnesses

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:43.260
the main antagonist of the game,

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.960
everyone's favorite geometric
ghoul, Pyramid Head,

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:49.440
doing something to two pairs
of legs stitched together.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.150
Look, we'll get to that, anyway,

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:54.560
he then meets a woman who looks
identical to his wife Mary,

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.380
but weirdly named Maria,

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:58.640
who tags along in hopes
of escaping the town.

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:00.030
After exploring a hospital

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:01.870
with questionable health standards,

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:03.730
Maria is killed by Pyramid Head,

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:06.880
only to be found inexplicably
alive a little later.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:08.710
James further explores Silent Hill,

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:11.730
repeatedly rescuing Maria
and watching her die,

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:14.150
rescuing Angela and watching her die,

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:16.320
trying to help Eddie
and having to kill him,

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.870
all while that little jerk
Laura keeps trying to kill him.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:22.280
This all culminates in
James confronting his past.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:25.010
Turns out, he euthanized/murdered his wife

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:27.480
as she was wasting away
from a terminal illness.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.850
Both to put her out of her misery

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:30.870
and so he might move on with his life.

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:32.670
Depending on how you play the game,

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:34.510
James can either leave Silent Hill

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:37.690
with the wife doppelganger
Maria, leave the town with Laura,

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:40.760
revive his dead wife using
the evil powers of the town,

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:44.220
or take his own life after
being torn apart by guilt.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:47.580
Silent Hill 2 is as tragic as it is scary.

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.990
Sure, the lighting and
the isolating atmosphere

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:52.490
makes wandering the empty
streets creepy as hell.

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:54.890
And yes, waiting for your
radio to fill with static

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:56.900
as another shambling nightmare approaches

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:58.580
can be unbearably tense.

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:02.180
But it's James' tragic backstory
that makes it all so bleak.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:04.360
To understand how the tragedy and scares

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:06.520
worked so cohesively, we have to turn

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:09.380
to Swiss psychoanalyst, Carl Jung,

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:12.330
a one time pupil of
mother-loving Sigmund Freud,

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:14.040
Jung believed human neuroses

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.620
are born out of the
subconscious which is influenced

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:17.560
by our desires.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.190
He thought of this subconscious desire

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:21.410
as a type of energy, a
sort of driving force

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:23.510
that he referred to as libido.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:25.450
This was different from Freud's definition

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:28.320
which was explicitly sexual
like everything with Freud.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:31.057
As Jung put it, "libido denotes a desire

00:03:31.057 --> 00:03:34.287
"or impulse unchecked by
any kind of authority,

00:03:34.287 --> 00:03:35.647
"moral or otherwise.

00:03:35.647 --> 00:03:38.470
"Libido is appetite in its natural state."

00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:40.040
Jung believed our psyche was a

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:43.210
self regulating system and
our libido is part of that.

00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:46.228
Our libidinal energy or drive simply knows

00:03:46.228 --> 00:03:48.540
where it should go to help the psyche,

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:49.717
likening it to water.

00:03:49.717 --> 00:03:53.007
"The libido has, as it
were, a natural penchant.

00:03:53.007 --> 00:03:55.507
"It is like water, which
must have a gradient

00:03:55.507 --> 00:03:56.630
"if it is to flow."

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:59.530
But just like water,
it can meet resistance

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:00.363
and back up.

00:04:00.363 --> 00:04:02.150
For Jung, this is what depression is,

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:04.120
a sort of clog in our libido.

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:07.130
So, our desires or libido
shows us where to go

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:09.910
but we have to do the work
to pull out that clog.

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:12.060
This concept is the first
step in understanding

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:14.090
the main premise of the game.

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:16.130
Most people, quite rightly, wonder why

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:18.480
James would go all the
way to spooky Silent Hill

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.580
in the first place when he knows damn well

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:21.790
his wife is dead.

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:23.570
You know, because he killed her.

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:25.860
We might also ask why as soon as he sees

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:28.210
the first half melted
figure move to attack him,

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:29.500
he doesn't just turn tail

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:31.830
and run right back the way he came in.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:33.450
After all, in some endings, he just

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:35.130
strolls right back out of town.

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:36.620
No doors lock shut behind him,

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:38.280
no fallen rocks block his path.

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:40.740
He even has an abundant supply of maps.

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:42.780
Instead, James stays because of his

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:45.650
subconscious desire, his desire to know

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:47.450
who sent the letter but mostly,

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:49.000
his desire for forgiveness.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.270
This is James's libido in action.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:53.000
Pushing him in the directions towards

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.320
what he desires most

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:55.840
and encouraging him to work through

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:57.410
the traumas that are clogging up

00:04:57.410 --> 00:04:59.270
the natural flow of his libido.

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:02.050
And that starts before he's
even set foot in the town.

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:04.240
Once he's there, the Jungian psychology

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.020
kicks into overdrive.

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:08.020
Not long after arriving in the town,

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:09.380
through a graveyard, I might add,

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:11.970
James encounters a monster
walking on two legs

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:14.080
but with no arms and no face.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.370
Though, it must have a mouth because

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:16.660
it likes to throw up on him.

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:17.970
Another type of monster you meet

00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:20.800
has two sets of legs stitched
on top of each other,

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.520
an anatomical oddity that might

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:24.380
in any other scenario seem goofy

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:25.550
instead of terrifying.

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:27.610
Part of this terror is driven by how

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:29.110
they're introduced along with the

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:31.220
breakout star of the
Silent Hill franchise,

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:32.100
Pyramid Head.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:34.300
While searching a hallway,
James hears a commotion

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.170
in one of the rooms.

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:37.580
He runs inside and then
ducks into a closet

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:40.220
where he peers through the
blinds to see what is happening

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:41.420
and what is happening?

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:42.580
Geez.

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:44.600
When Pyramid Head's not terrorizing you,

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:46.500
he's jamming a long spear or huge sword

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:47.950
into women's bodies.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:51.410
And yeah, you can probably see
where we're going with this.

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:53.649
Silent Hill 2 is full
of the types of symbols

00:05:53.649 --> 00:05:56.180
Jungian psychoanalysts
would love to decode.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:57.810
Jung's theory of symbolism was that

00:05:57.810 --> 00:06:00.010
certain primal energy is like love

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:02.840
and fear manifest in
our psyche as symbols.

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:04.550
Sometimes these symbols are specific,

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:06.050
a hammer you banged your thumb with

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:08.630
could become a symbol of
your pain or stupidity.

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:10.670
But sometimes these symbols are shared

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:11.840
between all people

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:14.840
and are as primal as the
energies they represent.

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:17.110
Jung called these kind
of symbols archetypes,

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:18.580
a phrase you might have heard before.

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:20.570
- A patient suffering delusional episodes

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:24.780
often focus their paranoia
on an external tormentor,

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:27.140
usually one conforming
to Jungian archetypes.

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:28.890
- [Michael] These
archetypes represent figures

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:30.920
and characters we see throughout history

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:32.820
in different cultures in civilization.

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:35.590
For Jung, the mother is an
archetype in every culture

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:37.790
and most religions all over the world

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:40.560
symbolizing fertility,
the earth, and compassion.

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:42.670
While he saw the wise old man archetype

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:45.350
as similarly the symbol of age, wisdom,

00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:47.040
and guidance in a lot of cultures.

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:49.440
Now, whether these symbols
are actually universal

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:50.600
has been contested.

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:52.010
But we're just sticking with Jung's model

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:52.880
for this video.

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:55.500
Whatever form they take,
these symbols express

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:57.418
a fundamental aspect of our psyche

00:06:57.418 --> 00:07:00.080
that we have trouble
consciously articulating.

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:02.917
Per Jung, "every psychological expression

00:07:02.917 --> 00:07:05.247
"is a symbol if we assume that it states

00:07:05.247 --> 00:07:07.087
"or signifies something more

00:07:07.087 --> 00:07:09.127
"and other than itself which eludes

00:07:09.127 --> 00:07:10.840
"our present knowledge."

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:12.200
In the case of Silent Hill,

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.050
we are able to diagnose a lot of

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:15.870
what is going on in James's head

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.790
just through the symbolism in the game.

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:20.790
Though some of these symbols
are obvious, some aren't.

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:23.900
So, let's get all Jungian
and psychoanalyze James.

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:27.360
And apologies in advance, this
might get a little graphic.

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:29.390
Don't blame us, blame Kanami.

00:07:29.390 --> 00:07:31.840
Let's start with the most
obvious symbol, Maria.

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:34.830
She is an exact likeness
of James's dead wife.

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:38.180
But more seductively dressed
and aggressively flirtatious.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:39.930
At the end of the game, James confesses

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:42.100
he was frustrated and angry with Mary

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:43.560
because he wanted to move on with his life

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:45.260
instead of having to care for her.

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:48.390
- [James] The truth is,
part of me hated you

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:51.550
for taking away my life.

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:53.520
- So, when James arrives in a haunted town

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:55.700
and meets his wife's near identical twin

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:57.770
with a similar name who is more assertive

00:07:57.770 --> 00:08:00.070
and sexually alluring, we begin to realize

00:08:00.070 --> 00:08:02.220
she represents not what his wife was

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:04.230
but what he might have wanted her to be.

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:06.630
Knowing this, we realize James's libido

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:09.580
might be as sexual as
Freud believed after all.

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:13.030
So, if Maria symbolizes the frustration

00:08:13.030 --> 00:08:14.968
James felt during his wife's long illness,

00:08:14.968 --> 00:08:17.110
that puts into context a lot of other

00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:19.030
symbols he encounters throughout the game.

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:20.730
Like Pyramid Head for instance.

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:22.460
James says at the end of the game,

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:26.360
- [James] That's why I needed you.

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:28.800
I needed someone to punish me for my sins.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:32.240
- Suggesting he or the
town created Pyramid Head

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:34.180
in an attempt at self-flagellation.

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:36.340
But while that might be
the monster's purpose,

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:38.670
what he symbolizes ties into James's

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:40.020
sexual frustration.

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:42.760
Like when we see the muscular
unstoppable powerhouse

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:45.600
stabbing his wife's lookalike
with a huge, long spear

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:48.090
and look, guys, we don't want to get

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:51.110
demonetized but you know what
we're talking about, right?

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:53.320
This kind of overt sexual symbolism

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:55.150
is consistent throughout the game.

00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:56.610
Seen in the nurse in the hospital

00:08:56.610 --> 00:08:58.820
wearing inexplicably revealing outfits

00:08:58.820 --> 00:09:00.740
or those freaky sets of women's legs

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:03.190
that are literally
attacking you with their,

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:04.310
well, you get it.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:06.040
And it's not just the monsters either.

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:07.950
The image in the frame when you see Angela

00:09:07.950 --> 00:09:09.810
for the final time is a corrupted

00:09:09.810 --> 00:09:12.420
representation of a naked female body.

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:14.130
Before that you find her in a room

00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:16.470
that has walls seemingly made of flesh.

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:18.660
Also, there are orifices above your head

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:22.130
with cylinders sliding
repeatedly in and out.

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:24.270
At other times, the monsters symbolize

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:26.840
a less sexual version of James's guilt.

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:28.630
The first monsters you meet resemble

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:30.000
a person in a straight jacket.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.010
This is before you find all the notes

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:34.120
about violent patients in the asylum.

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:36.060
For James, who we learned felt trapped

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:37.730
in his marriage to a dying woman,

00:09:37.730 --> 00:09:40.640
the symbol of a visibly
bound creature attacking him

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:42.520
can be seen as a symbol
of the restrictions

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:44.300
he felt while caring for his wife.

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:46.501
The final boss of the
game amounts to a surreal

00:09:46.501 --> 00:09:48.130
nightmare version of Mary,

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:50.490
or Maria, depending on
how you played the game,

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:52.850
strapped in a bed hanging over James.

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:54.960
This image of a woman bound to her bed

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:58.210
floating above him, literally
hanging over his head

00:09:58.210 --> 00:10:00.390
as it hinders him symbolizes how James

00:10:00.390 --> 00:10:02.320
felt about his wife as she was dying.

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:05.230
An oppressive presence
following him wherever he goes

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:07.430
that he ultimately ends up destroying.

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:09.090
The other people driven to the town

00:10:09.090 --> 00:10:11.130
by their libidinal energy are struggling

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:12.530
with their own demons too.

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:15.054
Early on in the game, James
reads a note that says,

00:10:15.054 --> 00:10:16.990
I saw those demons.

00:10:16.990 --> 00:10:18.310
They were there, I'm certain.

00:10:18.310 --> 00:10:20.630
But my friend says he didn't see anything.

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:22.300
If that's true, does that mean

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:24.320
that what I saw was an illusion?

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:26.340
The more we talk to the other characters,

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:27.947
especially Eddie and Angela,

00:10:27.947 --> 00:10:30.740
we realize they might
see things that we don't

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:31.830
and vice versa.

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:34.430
Not only do characters
not see what you see

00:10:34.430 --> 00:10:36.710
but mention seeing their own visions.

00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:38.303
- [Eddie] Red pyramid thing?

00:10:39.163 --> 00:10:41.580
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:10:41.580 --> 00:10:42.687
Honest.

00:10:42.687 --> 00:10:45.320
But I did see some weird looking monsters.

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:47.180
- [Michael] They also
exhibit bizarre behavior

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:50.090
best explained by experiencing
some other reality.

00:10:50.090 --> 00:10:52.230
Eddie who admits to maiming a bully

00:10:52.230 --> 00:10:54.530
and killing a dog before he attacks you

00:10:54.530 --> 00:10:56.820
- [Eddie] Yeah, I killed that dog.

00:10:56.820 --> 00:10:57.790
It was fun.

00:10:57.790 --> 00:10:59.490
- [Michael] He is seen nonchalantly

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:01.480
eating a pizza earlier on in the game,

00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:04.360
right after you found him
throwing up into a toilet bowl.

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:06.630
Angela, who we discovered
killed her father

00:11:06.630 --> 00:11:08.570
in self defense when he assaulted her.

00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:10.710
- Go ahead and say it!

00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:13.107
Or you could just force me.

00:11:13.107 --> 00:11:16.800
Beat me up like he always did.

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:18.670
- [Michael] Flips between
barely noticing you

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:20.350
and being terrified.

00:11:20.350 --> 00:11:22.932
She even mistakes you for
her mother at the end.

00:11:22.932 --> 00:11:24.477
- Mama!

00:11:24.477 --> 00:11:26.300
Mama, I was looking for you!

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:27.460
- [Michael] But before she disappears

00:11:27.460 --> 00:11:28.968
into the flames, she says,

00:11:28.968 --> 00:11:30.590
- [Angela] You see it too?

00:11:30.590 --> 00:11:33.730
For me, it's always like this.

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:35.660
- [Michael] All of their strange behaviors

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:37.240
paint that these characters are also

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:39.030
going through their own traumas.

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:41.000
Implying that Silent Hill could be

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:43.720
manifesting each person's own demons.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:46.410
Just like James, they
have a libidinal desire

00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:48.800
which has been clogged
by trauma from their past

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:50.660
and has brought them there to work through

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:53.340
these issues but because
we are playing as James,

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:55.500
we don't know exactly what their traumas

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:58.730
or desires are and can
only see what he sees.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:00.240
But how does all of this psychology

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:01.820
also make it so scary?

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:04.110
There aren't really any
jump scares in the game.

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:05.980
These symbols simply show you what

00:12:05.980 --> 00:12:07.570
is going on in James's head without

00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:08.610
needing to explain it.

00:12:08.610 --> 00:12:11.700
And this is why a lot
of the more recent games

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:14.000
and the movie, in
particular, missed the point.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:15.580
Instead of exploring the psychology

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:17.570
of their main characters,
they simply recycle

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:19.140
the imagery from Silent Hill 2

00:12:19.140 --> 00:12:21.500
that bears no relation to the protagonist,

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:23.380
meaning they don't symbolize anything.

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:25.130
They're still scary but don't have the

00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:26.970
same effect or significance.

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:28.730
In the movie, the character of Rose

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:30.430
is searching for her adopted daughter

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:31.910
who is lost in Silent Hill.

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:34.130
While you could argue
the creepy baby monsters

00:12:34.130 --> 00:12:36.220
might be some sort of symbol for Rose's

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:38.920
maternal instincts, what
does Pyramid Head symbolize?

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:40.090
Or the sexy nurses?

00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:43.400
Silent Hill 2 is still
so rewarding by contrast

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:46.550
because of another of Jung's
psychological processes

00:12:46.550 --> 00:12:48.080
he called the cathartic method.

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:49.780
This is the method of becoming conscious

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:51.570
of repressed feelings or trauma

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:53.630
through the retelling or reliving of it.

00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:55.870
Also known as abreaction.

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:59.530
One then confesses so
as to heal and move on.

00:12:59.530 --> 00:13:01.577
As Jung describes it, "the goal of the

00:13:01.577 --> 00:13:03.877
"Cathartic Method is full confession.

00:13:03.877 --> 00:13:05.937
"Not merely the intellectual recognition

00:13:05.937 --> 00:13:07.307
"of the facts with the head,

00:13:07.307 --> 00:13:09.187
"but their confirmation by the heart

00:13:09.187 --> 00:13:12.000
"and the actual release
of suppressed emotion."

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.920
It's this form of catharsis
that Silent Hill 2

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:16.350
captures perfectly.

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:18.100
After James watches the video tape

00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:19.690
of him smothering his wife,

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:21.910
the player finally understands his guilt.

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:24.520
The traumatic clog that his libido drove

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:26.680
him to the town to fix in the first place

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:29.530
and the meaning behind all
the gross, sexy monsters.

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:31.120
No matter what ending you get,

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:33.240
it is satisfying because they all feature

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:35.570
a confrontation with his memory of Mary

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:37.240
and a reading of her final letter to him

00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:39.800
explaining her feelings before she dies.

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:43.033
- [Mary] I feel so pathetic
and ugly laying here,

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:45.320
waiting for you.

00:13:45.320 --> 00:13:46.250
- [Michael] It is only when James

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:48.330
confronts these symbols of his guilt

00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:50.160
that the game can finally end.

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:52.470
It provides a kind of catharsis for James

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:54.290
and as a result, the player.

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:57.320
This is why Silent Hill
is still a horror classic,

00:13:57.320 --> 00:13:59.140
not just because you probably played it

00:13:59.140 --> 00:14:00.440
when you were too young.

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:02.610
But because it uses actual psychology

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:05.630
and Jungian psychoanalysis
to get into your head.

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:07.410
The town scares its characters by

00:14:07.410 --> 00:14:10.240
understanding what drives
them there in the first place.

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:11.830
Their libido that forces them to

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:13.380
confront their past traumas.

00:14:13.380 --> 00:14:15.170
It then plays on those fears and traumas,

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:17.040
and because we have come to sympathize

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:18.780
with James and co throughout the game,

00:14:18.780 --> 00:14:20.730
it scares the player too.

00:14:20.730 --> 00:14:23.140
It takes what James is already afraid of

00:14:23.140 --> 00:14:24.930
and represents it symbolically

00:14:24.930 --> 00:14:27.610
so that when his inner and
outer demons are defeated,

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:29.730
or not, depending on your in game choices,

00:14:29.730 --> 00:14:32.060
James's story is a cathartic experience

00:14:32.060 --> 00:14:34.520
about closure and coming
to terms with loss

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:37.480
and sex, a lot of it is about sex.

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:40.637
In short, it takes this quote
from Oscar Wilde literally.

00:14:40.637 --> 00:14:42.567
"We are each our own devil,

00:14:42.567 --> 00:14:44.970
"and we make this world our hell."

00:14:44.970 --> 00:14:46.060
But what do you think?

00:14:46.060 --> 00:14:47.410
Let us know in the comments.

00:14:47.410 --> 00:14:49.570
A big old thanks to our awesome patrons

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:51.970
for supporting our
podcast and the channel.

00:14:51.970 --> 00:14:54.270
Go ahead and hit that subscribe button,

00:14:54.270 --> 00:14:56.440
and as always, thanks for watching.

00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:58.370
Don't have nightmares, Wisecrack.

00:14:58.370 --> 00:14:59.203
Peace.

00:14:59.203 --> 00:15:01.692
(upbeat music)

